Voxel Grid Transformation Math (2D Array to 3D World Space)Your map layout is calculated as a flat 2D grid matrix (\(M\)), but your player walks in an absolute 3D Cartesian coordinates space \((X, Y, Z)\). To transition between these two spaces without lag, the engine uses matrix transformation equations.Center Origin Translation FormulaBy default, array indices start at \((0,0)\) in the top-left corner. If you spawn tiles starting at zero, your map expands outward into one quadrant, breaking lighting and clipping coordinates. To center a 1000×1000 map around the absolute engine center \((0,0,0)\), use this linear transformation formula:\(X=\left(c\cdot S\right)-\left(\frac{W\cdot S}{2}\right)\)\(Z=\left(r\cdot S\right)-\left(\frac{H\cdot S}{2}\right)\)\(c, r\) = The current column and row indices in your data array.\(W, H\) = Total width and height boundaries of your grid layout (\(1000 \times 1000\)).\(S\) = CELL_SIZE scaling factor (\(64\) units in your codebase).\(Y\) = Height offset. Floors sit at \(Y = 0\); walls are shifted to \(Y = \frac{S}{2}\) so their bases rest cleanly on the ground plane.2. Natural Terrain & Chaos Math (Fractal Noise)To prevent your palace rooms or coastlines from looking blocky and unnatural, a 2D pseudo-random generation function creates unpredictable yet continuous waves.Fractional Brownian Motion (fBm)Instead of using a single random check, the terrain generator calculates Fractal Brownian Motion by layering multiple frequencies (octaves) of Perlin or Simplex noise algorithms together:\(f(x,z)=\sum _{i=0}^{n-1}a_{i}\cdot \text{Noise}(f_{i}\cdot x,\,f_{i}\cdot z)\)Where each progressive octave layer modifies the variables dynamically:Amplitude (\(a_{i}\)): Controls the height/extremity of the features. It decreases each layer: \(a_i = \text{persistence}^i\).Frequency (\(f_{i}\)): Controls the granular detail frequency. It increases each layer: \(f_i = \text{lacunarity}^i\).If the output value of \(f(x, z) > \text{threshold}\), the code assigns a TILE_WALL (\(1\)). If it falls below, it carves a open path TILE_FLOOR (\(2\)).3. High-Performance Render Optimization MathLooping through a \(1000 \times 1000\) matrix yields up to 1,000,000 potential coordinate indexes. If you try to create a unique 3D mesh object for every single tile, the browser script execution will instantly crash.Affine Transformation MatricesTo handle this scale inside an HTML5 WebGL context, Three.js uses InstancedMesh allocation. This system uploads a single master geometry asset to the GPU alongside a giant flattened array of 16-element transformation matrices (\(T\)), drawing all blocks in a single high-speed draw call:\(T=\left[\begin{matrix}m_{11}&m_{12}&m_{13}&X\\ m_{21}&m_{22}&m_{23}&Y\\ m_{31}&m_{32}&m_{33}&Z\\ 0&0&0&1\end{matrix}\right]\)The \(3 \times 3\) upper-left quadrant handles your asset scale metrics (stretching the base geometry out to match your uniform \(64\)-unit CELL_SIZE configuration).The rightmost column vector \((X, Y, Z)\) injects your precise grid translation values directly into hardware acceleration memory.